+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Design analysis for the combo variant
+#
+# a) Concrete behavior and trace:
+#    - The base task used an open funnel: the opening itself revealed the
+#      outward direction, and the outward corridor was only implicit.
+#    - This combo removes the visible opening. The wall becomes a sealed
+#      rectangular shell around one cavity. Exactly one of the four sides is
+#      1-pixel thick; the other three sides are 2-3 pixels thick.
+#    - The fill seed still sits inside the cavity near the side opposite the
+#      future exit. The solver must first recover the whole cavity by flood-fill
+#      from the seed, then compare the four side thicknesses, then choose the
+#      unique thinnest side as the break direction.
+#    - After the break, the fill travels outward as a straight rectangular beam.
+#      The D8 part changes what becomes visible there: two wall-colored border
+#      lines are extended alongside the beam so the beam is wrapped inside a
+#      pipe instead of floating in open background.
+#    - Small trace:
+#      original: open U facing up -> endpoints say "up" -> fill climbs out.
+#      combo: closed shell with top thickness 1 and other sides thickness 2-3
+#      -> fill floods cavity -> top wall strip is breached -> fill rises in a
+#      rectangle -> two vertical wall lines appear on the left/right edges of
+#      that rectangle, so the outgoing ray becomes a pipe.
+#
+# b) Complexity calibration:
+#    - The combo keeps only four directional cases, one per cardinal side.
+#    - The thin-wall signal is repeated across an entire side, not a single
+#      pixel cue, which makes the comparison visually robust.
+#    - The pipe extension is also repeated twice per sample as a matched pair of
+#      parallel border lines; this is strong enough for human inference without
+#      introducing many categories or special cases.
+#
+# c) Hidden assumptions that changed:
+#    - Endpoint detection from the original solver no longer applies because the
+#      main wall is a loop, not an open chain.
+#    - Reachability cannot start from an already open corridor; the cavity must
+#      stay sealed in the input and be reconstructed from the seed.
+#    - The outward geometry is no longer just fill. Some output cells that were
+#      background in the input must become wall-color pipe borders.
+#    - Obstacle placement must avoid those future pipe-border cells, otherwise
+#      preserved obstacles would clash with newly painted wall extensions.
